@section kfc_intro Introduction
This document describes the usage of the AUFIT program. AUFIT is the acronym for Atari 
Universal Floppy-Disk Image Tool. 

The program can read many Floppy Disk image's formats 
used with the Atari platform including images generated at the flux level by devices like 
SuperCard Pro, KryoFlux, and Discovery Cartridge. Once read the FD image can be analyzed 
and the content can be displayed using Graphical and Text outputs. 

It is also possible to output the information read to several image formats. It is 
therefore possible to use the program to convert from one format to another. 

Usage has been designed to be as simple as possible for casual users. However 
the program also provides powerful features for advanced users.

@section _proguse Program Usage

Currently the program does not requires to be installed and is provided directly 
as an executable: Aufit.exe. To run the program just double click the executable.

The program run under Windows Vista SP2, Windows 7 SP1, and Widows 8 or above. 
The program requires that the Microsoft.NET Framework 4.5 or above is installed. 
It also requires the Ookii Dialogs class library. The Ookii DLL is provided along 
with the executable and documentation.

This documentation is primarily for developers.
For more information please refer to Aufit User's Manual.
Enjoy

@author	Jean Louis-Guerin

